(PCB Fabrication Recommendation) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (The current PCB is designed as a 4-layer board. Due ) Tj
T* (to the impedance-control and reference-plane continuity ) Tj
T* (requirements of the high-speed signals routed on the ) Tj
T* (bottom layer, a 6-layer stack-up is recommended for ) Tj
T* (prototype fabrication, with Layer 5 implemented as a ) Tj
T* (complete and continuous ground plane.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (The solid Layer 5 ground plane provides a stable ) Tj
T* (reference plane and return path for the bottom-layer) Tj
T* (high-speed signals, improving impedance matching and ) Tj
T* (reducing signal-integrity and EMI risks. Before fabrication,) Tj
T* (confirm the final stack-up with the PCB manufacturer and) Tj
T* (recalculate the trace widths and spacing according to the) Tj
T* (specified target impedance.) Tj
